  'Students learn that editing is not only technical assembly; it is the central language of time, attention, emotion, causality, and meaning in moving images.',
  $edpojson${"slug": "editing-and-post-production", "title": "Editing and Post-Production", "description": "Students learn that editing is not only technical assembly; it is the central language of time, attention, emotion, causality, and meaning in moving images.", "topics": [{"id": "20798afc-aadb-4a2a-b8fd-ec1d204d01a6", "type": "topic", "title": "Editing as Cinematic Language", "description": "Students learn that editing is not only technical assembly; it is the central language of time, attention, emotion, causality, and meaning in moving images.", "children": [{"id": "59aef3e6-2deb-42d6-8a7a-6d7c0d3af5eb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "The grammar of the cut", "children": [{"id": "c28f27b4-5f75-45db-98b9-78e5077ad56c", "type": "concept", "title": "Shot, take, setup, sequence, scene, transition, and ellipsis"}, {"id": "3f698e01-f16f-4cac-b227-322707dc7f22", "type": "concept", "title": "Cut on action, match cut, jump cut, smash cut, L-cut, J-cut, and dissolve"}, {"id": "3227549d-65d0-4a04-abf1-dad67c844a73", "type": "concept", "title": "Screen direction, eyeline, point of view, emphasis, and narrative clarity"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces the cut as a meaningful relation between shots, not just a way to remove unwanted footage."}, {"id": "7f5bc54d-e55f-4510-af05-850176c703a1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Time, duration, and attention", "children": [{"id": "8b5d6905-2d77-4e15-b3f3-f29b01226235", "type": "concept", "title": "Real time, compressed time, expanded time, flashback, flashforward, and parallel action"}, {"id": "67e5933a-beae-47da-9b8b-b8c4c8190627", "type": "concept", "title": "Attention management, withholding, reveal, surprise, suspense, and expectation"}, {"id": "863faab3-dd6b-4a78-b730-48f827a26065", "type": "concept", "title": "Rhythmic density, visual contrast, and perceptual load"}], "description": "Students learn how editors compress, expand, reorder, and guide time so viewers feel story rather than merely receive information."}, {"id": "3db9b235-2a14-4b9d-a765-502ffc837b0b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Meaning through relation", "children": [{"id": "505191a4-bbf3-421f-92e5-11e98c12dfb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Kuleshov effect, montage theory, intellectual montage, and associative editing"}, {"id": "787b0b79-b0f0-4ece-a033-4c9e23b43436", "type": "concept", "title": "Emotional, spatial, graphic, rhythmic, and thematic relationships"}, {"id": "0e0b11b2-1a23-411d-9c19-53a5f4937fbb", "type": "concept", "title": "When clarity matters and when productive ambiguity matters"}], "description": "This section shows how meaning often emerges between shots through juxtaposition, association, and audience inference."}]}, {"id": "87216c16-cf93-4144-9352-b2ed645a5c97", "type": "topic", "title": "Story Analysis, Dailies, Coverage, and Editorial Judgment", "description": "Students learn how editors read footage, diagnose story problems, evaluate performances, and form a plan before building a cut.", "children": [{"id": "aee28908-0357-4089-b5a7-1372f6fb9ef6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reading footage critically", "children": [{"id": "d3bf35d2-0913-4311-b44f-c324ca128335", "type": "concept", "title": "Dailies review, circle takes, continuity notes, script supervisor notes, and director comments"}, {"id": "8cc2544d-da4e-4859-b9b5-94e4cf7bc790", "type": "concept", "title": "Performance, blocking, camera movement, focus, exposure, sound, and usability"}, {"id": "c433a866-0597-4195-acf8-1a6b3a326fdc", "type": "concept", "title": "Discovering story opportunities, missing beats, and unexpected strengths"}], "description": "The goal is to see what the footage can actually do, not what the script or shoot plan hoped it would do."}, {"id": "3c2eda19-d51a-477d-9926-7159aa9bd119", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Coverage and scene options", "children": [{"id": "59fde2b3-8c0b-4bba-b8e0-ace814be581a", "type": "concept", "title": "Masters, singles, over-the-shoulders, inserts, cutaways, reaction shots, and wild lines"}, {"id": "f5e9bf99-2e86-4102-9855-5e174ccf02f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Beat mapping, emotional turns, entrances, exits, and scene objectives"}, {"id": "c1aa0ff0-d5c5-4334-abb4-fb65479f5626", "type": "concept", "title": "Using coverage to solve pacing, clarity, continuity, and performance problems"}], "description": "Students learn to assess coverage as a set of storytelling possibilities and constraints."}, {"id": "25d469d0-e1c3-4daa-bb81-5ba0afa2efa6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Editorial judgment", "children": [{"id": "a15564f0-ba7b-43e6-9127-e24419351f0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Intention, point of view, tone, stakes, character alignment, and audience empathy"}, {"id": "c70dadf7-4338-4e9e-9bf2-f5ad53d7185b", "type": "concept", "title": "Cutting for story over favorite shots, beautiful images, or technical perfection"}, {"id": "b28cdc43-c7a3-4ba9-946a-ebbcc5431205", "type": "concept", "title": "Making defensible creative decisions and explaining them in critique"}], "description": "This subtopic frames editing as a sequence of choices about story priority, audience experience, and collaboration."}]}, {"id": "50a6eee4-b198-4f11-b4c6-6e1e1ec7e5aa", "type": "topic", "title": "Nonlinear Editing Workflow and Assistant Editor Foundations", "description": "Students build professional habits for ingesting, organizing, syncing, backing up, editing, and handing off media in modern NLE environments.", "children": [{"id": "603564da-1ace-485d-b335-37ea801f2dca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project setup and media management", "children": [{"id": "1114e33d-440e-4416-b25b-3125f95030c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Folder structures, project settings, naming conventions, bins, markers, and metadata"}, {"id": "01e2c145-b7c1-41d5-9ac5-371585849476", "type": "concept", "title": "Camera originals, proxies, transcoding, optimized media, relinking, and offline/online workflow"}, {"id": "590a174b-319a-4290-92c7-a7824192c29c", "type": "concept", "title": "3-2-1 backup thinking, checksums, drive management, and version control"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches the invisible organization that keeps creative editing from becoming technical chaos."}, {"id": "a2c57ab8-cba3-49d7-8c7d-a972d2ae325f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sync, selects, and assistant workflows", "children": [{"id": "b66cc044-d97c-4039-b32b-452e74f9748f", "type": "concept", "title": "Audio sync, multicam sync, slates, timecode, waveform sync, and grouped clips"}, {"id": "d0c4c2fd-e32e-4620-a172-3d0f4e873a05", "type": "concept", "title": "Selects reels, stringouts, scene bins, script sync, markers, and annotations"}, {"id": "8767dc72-0d5a-48cc-a5e4-e528b2fb404d", "type": "concept", "title": "Turnover prep, EDL/XML/AAF/OMF basics, project sharing, and handoff etiquette"}], "description": "Students learn the assistant editor practices that make an edit room fast, reliable, and collaborative."}, {"id": "97af2f3c-6b5c-43a7-b3ae-0f8183d208c7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional NLE fluency", "children": [{"id": "4b360631-4048-463e-910a-8b4228a12bcf", "type": "concept", "title": "Timelines, tracks, nesting, multicam, source/record editing, trimming, and keyboard shortcuts"}, {"id": "d1368785-9474-4299-adcc-80016b2aa171", "type": "concept", "title": "Effects pipelines, adjustment layers, speed changes, stabilization, and basic compositing"}, {"id": "c58bbde6-c78a-412a-a01d-0dfedc9b1f8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Export settings, render management, project cleanup, and troubleshooting"}], "description": "The course treats software as a craft environment: students should understand concepts that transfer across Premiere, Resolve, Avid, and Final Cut."}]}, {"id": "590b9356-d249-429b-90b5-689ee1bdf78a", "type": "topic", "title": "Continuity Editing, Spatial Clarity, and Performance Construction", "description": "Students learn classical continuity as a powerful system for clarity, then learn how and when to bend it.", "children": [{"id": "2238a403-2c89-4574-b343-bd3ea9182d04", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Classical continuity systems", "children": [{"id": "132088a6-a07b-4335-b80f-800ae2bf5e98", "type": "concept", "title": "180-degree rule, 30-degree rule, shot/reverse shot, eyeline match, and matching action"}, {"id": "d78df535-de18-4d6a-bc10-09d0320b1471", "type": "concept", "title": "Establishing geography, entrances and exits, eye traces, and screen direction"}, {"id": "4a9c87ec-0889-4e71-a856-1c34a4225f96", "type": "concept", "title": "Cutaways, inserts, reaction shots, and continuity repair"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches the conventions that help viewers understand space, action, and character intention without confusion."}, {"id": "1f76adc6-0556-474e-9b3e-ba538a5a41e8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Performance shaping", "children": [{"id": "f092a8b5-e27c-4371-a0ba-2ec8cd0ad86d", "type": "concept", "title": "Choosing takes for intention, listening, subtext, vulnerability, and energy"}, {"id": "1fd78cdd-f69a-4316-b882-956afcb67171", "type": "concept", "title": "Combining dialogue, pauses, reactions, overlaps, and breath"}, {"id": "9219139f-a3c4-4de8-aeb8-f96148345426", "type": "concept", "title": "Respecting actors while shaping the emotional truth of the scene"}], "description": "Students learn that editors often build performances from many takes, pauses, reactions, and rhythms."}, {"id": "14e62d5e-ef98-4e6e-844d-6320261cb1ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Breaking continuity with purpose", "children": [{"id": "1e811b7e-7692-4c26-b0a3-3c5113657528", "type": "concept", "title": "Jump cuts, temporal fragmentation, subjective editing, and spatial disorientation"}, {"id": "14a76689-5254-4b99-b4ca-c20da3cc85fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Experimental, comedic, horror, action, documentary, and music-video uses"}, {"id": "b9a17d03-be42-4749-a9ff-3b74f9270fb1", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience contract, genre expectation, and intentional rule breaking"}], "description": "This section helps students distinguish expressive discontinuity from accidental confusion."}]}, {"id": "d04516f4-7452-4822-ba18-11533a6aa990", "type": "topic", "title": "Rhythm, Pacing, Scene Shape, and Emotional Momentum", "description": "Students develop the editor's ear for timing: when to cut, when to hold, when to breathe, and when to accelerate.", "children": [{"id": "cabca284-0e8c-4ec4-8481-e2b2e514c41e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pacing and scene architecture", "children": [{"id": "76d8c975-eb5d-43e2-bbf9-6ec373d1eda8", "type": "concept", "title": "Opening beat, inciting pressure, reversals, reveals, climax, and button"}, {"id": "c4ade5bd-c11c-4c9e-a0b0-686b92d4924c", "type": "concept", "title": "Scene length, silence, pauses, overlaps, and visual breathing room"}, {"id": "525449dd-ef02-4a69-9199-e39b52f72ae0", "type": "concept", "title": "Cutting entrances, exits, repetition, dead air, and redundant information"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches students to shape scenes around beats, turns, escalation, and release."}, {"id": "0b850bae-7dd4-4fbb-8acf-65057437e60f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rhythm across image and sound", "children": [{"id": "ffb0c367-1972-4613-87e6-3ae97f2cb8b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Internal rhythm, external rhythm, musical rhythm, visual rhythm, and dialogue rhythm"}, {"id": "08450179-5238-4513-8667-9b0cc9044f61", "type": "concept", "title": "Action cutting, comedy timing, horror timing, trailer pacing, and contemplative pacing"}, {"id": "0d4f0e91-9849-4480-8c1e-116fafa78956", "type": "concept", "title": "Using sound bridges, reactions, and offscreen space to control rhythm"}], "description": "Students learn that rhythm is built from picture, performance, sound, music, camera movement, and audience expectation."}, {"id": "a7402a56-0371-4343-a71b-a3cfe99193f8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Emotional momentum", "children": [{"id": "643cbd12-c044-493a-93f9-61f3f8cad1d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Empathy, tension, release, dread, surprise, curiosity, and catharsis"}, {"id": "0abac05e-82dc-4127-a743-c8282a1fb453", "type": "concept", "title": "Point of view, identification, withheld information, and audience alignment"}, {"id": "9b9c61d3-a8c0-453e-98e6-913472f29e06", "type": "concept", "title": "When a slower cut is stronger than a faster cut"}], "description": "This section focuses on how edits create emotional direction rather than merely accelerate or shorten footage."}]}, {"id": "ae76aeb6-3c59-482f-a46b-c7b2be805872", "type": "topic", "title": "Montage, Juxtaposition, Time Compression, and Experimental Structure", "description": "Students study montage as a way to build ideas, memory, emotion, argument, and non-linear forms through collision and association.", "children": [{"id": "cea5e76b-4291-4d3c-9559-3724f4b57446", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Montage traditions", "children": [{"id": "9e609d9c-6e2b-4e39-9a25-b190d53ea46e", "type": "concept", "title": "Soviet montage, intellectual montage, metric montage, rhythmic montage, and tonal montage"}, {"id": "f19737f1-0518-4b33-8487-2766cd22f946", "type": "concept", "title": "Training montage, memory montage, essay film, music video, and advertising montage"}, {"id": "29b679e6-eb1b-477a-a2e2-52e0f7bcd2d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Associative logic, graphic match, contrast, repetition, and motif"}], "description": "This subtopic connects practical montage editing to major film traditions and theories."}, {"id": "5b4d5ab1-87f7-4e1d-9a3d-d885561fad9b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Temporal construction", "children": [{"id": "c8c2ed89-a416-4dc1-8343-5b39a7214451", "type": "concept", "title": "Compression, expansion, ellipsis, parallel editing, cross-cutting, and recurring timelines"}, {"id": "1b06d17e-fb21-4256-a66e-361b665dfc3b", "type": "concept", "title": "Flashbacks, subjective memory, dream logic, and unreliable chronology"}, {"id": "1c942829-1a3e-4392-a2a3-ca939c010612", "type": "concept", "title": "Using time jumps without losing viewer orientation"}], "description": "Students learn to build story time from fragments, ellipses, repetitions, and parallel structures."}, {"id": "ef189e48-2430-492b-9023-2f967621966d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Experimental and time-based media", "children": [{"id": "a3d4e74d-46f3-48d3-92c1-02f837e89b67", "type": "concept", "title": "Duration, loops, installation contexts, projection, monitors, and gallery presentation"}, {"id": "b2ee212a-c351-4f41-9ef4-028329d73e0a", "type": "concept", "title": "Non-narrative structure, abstraction, performance, documentation, and video art"}, {"id": "67de5951-3eaa-4464-b1a2-c49f993faf15", "type": "concept", "title": "Sound-image relationships, audience movement, and screening context"}], "description": "This section draws from MFA moving-image practice to expand editing beyond conventional narrative screen work."}]}, {"id": "e6ddce37-0d0b-45e4-a9bd-9ddf4f4febfd", "type": "topic", "title": "Documentary, Unscripted, Archival, and Ethical Editing", "description": "Students learn how nonfiction editors construct story while honoring consent, context, truthfulness, participants, and archival responsibility.", "children": [{"id": "3f7c50ee-7e6f-4bb7-a39a-3bd519d83816", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Documentary structure", "children": [{"id": "f03f4157-ce40-475e-88ee-ed8b2ac63eed", "type": "concept", "title": "Character arcs, themes, sequences, act structure, cards, narration, and interview paper cuts"}, {"id": "10199291-75a2-45f9-816a-3331e1bc0c76", "type": "concept", "title": "Verite scenes, observational footage, archival evidence, and found footage"}, {"id": "50dd93ca-7d38-4216-a7c9-022b70825678", "type": "concept", "title": "Balancing exposition, discovery, emotion, argument, and ambiguity"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches how documentary story is found and built from interviews, verite, archives, and unfolding reality."}, {"id": "94ca046a-4314-485d-82ad-32c78a69ae53", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interview and participant ethics", "children": [{"id": "45a5a5d8-ddc6-43f6-8fb0-7f4cb2d81759", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent, informed participation, trauma-aware editing, and participant accountability"}, {"id": "117f3108-ccc9-4ea4-ac9e-a78a48999357", "type": "concept", "title": "Context collapse, misleading juxtaposition, Frankenbites, and selective emphasis"}, {"id": "dc7a8087-2087-45ca-8d58-b1ab5a621537", "type": "concept", "title": "Duty of care, fair representation, review practices, and impact goals"}], "description": "Students learn the ethical weight of editing real people, trauma, memory, and testimony."}, {"id": "e1e57ad1-4f5d-4db6-b9a2-82b79b407d82", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Archival and fair-use workflows", "children": [{"id": "207e3a2d-34f8-463c-b0d4-7757472ac3ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Archival logs, source tracking, rights status, releases, citations, and licensing"}, {"id": "e58a1aa0-6a55-4d71-8e33-d81d163dbfed", "type": "concept", "title": "Stills, scans, news footage, home movies, social video, and found media"}, {"id": "33db4f0a-c1a2-4686-b4e1-218c0ab7304b", "type": "concept", "title": "Fair use reasoning, transformation, risk review, and deliverables documentation"}], "description": "This section grounds archival editing in research, provenance, rights, and visual storytelling."}]}, {"id": "6033310d-00d7-47a0-9a26-1df71b544463", "type": "topic", "title": "Sound Editing, Foley, Music, and Mix Preparation", "description": "Students learn how post sound shapes space, emotion, point of view, continuity, and professional polish.", "children": [{"id": "5bdb2bf8-4adf-4af4-b579-0e9310acb544", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dialogue editing and cleanup", "children": [{"id": "bf55c69b-cd8f-4046-b5c2-7e9dcd1dbd07", "type": "concept", "title": "Dialogue selects, room tone, ambience matching, noise reduction, de-clicking, and de-plosive work"}, {"id": "cef190fd-711d-4b73-b3c8-3685ed6afae0", "type": "concept", "title": "ADR basics, wild lines, sync, overlaps, and dialogue continuity"}, {"id": "2ad0eacb-bf80-4df8-afc2-927550c9d255", "type": "concept", "title": "Track organization, naming, handles, and mix handoff"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches the foundation of intelligible, emotionally coherent post audio."}, {"id": "73d9a981-17fb-4a51-a290-44f1a60a1775", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Foley, effects, ambience, and sound design", "children": [{"id": "40183796-54a2-428e-b4dc-edc8e10c3550", "type": "concept", "title": "Foley performance, footsteps, cloth, props, hard effects, and designed effects"}, {"id": "c53e1b35-a9b7-49fe-920c-dc03ab993db3", "type": "concept", "title": "Ambience, backgrounds, offscreen space, transitions, impacts, and sonic motifs"}, {"id": "768ed9ba-b122-45c3-9faa-242b5d022ec9", "type": "concept", "title": "Library workflow, recording, editing, layering, and sound perspective"}], "description": "Students use sound to make image worlds feel physical, subjective, and alive."}, {"id": "53c03293-d7ff-4894-80ed-8e57a111516e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Music and mix preparation", "children": [{"id": "bf8dd79a-278f-4648-b330-93babd4249b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Temp music, spotting, cue points, licensing, stems, and composer communication"}, {"id": "fae164f0-04fc-456a-a5cb-39d0e861335f", "type": "concept", "title": "Levels, panning, EQ basics, compression basics, and loudness awareness"}, {"id": "c82fb6b9-d8c8-40f4-aaa5-2044f0f9a89b", "type": "concept", "title": "Stems, M&E, deliverable splits, and communication with sound mixers"}], "description": "This subtopic helps students make music choices and prepare clean sessions for the final mix."}]}, {"id": "43c50ff2-e20c-43c0-991c-ba4a77a81f91", "type": "topic", "title": "Color Correction, Color Grading, and Image Finishing", "description": "Students learn the difference between technical correction and expressive grading, while building an image pipeline that survives handoff.", "children": [{"id": "156edaeb-4389-42d3-9acf-25bd0d7a1ed7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color correction fundamentals", "children": [{"id": "066bc9f1-c7d7-4f78-b381-b071fb922fd9", "type": "concept", "title": "Exposure, contrast, white balance, saturation, skin tone, scopes, and shot matching"}, {"id": "cc90cae0-72ac-4658-abf8-3f86e3bea437", "type": "concept", "title": "Log, RAW, LUTs, color management, gamma, gamut, and display transforms"}, {"id": "dabbe879-9503-4780-ba68-92df6a37b315", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary corrections, secondaries, masks, tracking, and noise reduction basics"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches students to make shots match and read correctly before stylizing them."}, {"id": "2475b90f-4a7f-4bff-9924-009695a44f8a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Creative grading", "children": [{"id": "c833624e-a9a0-4d5f-8e0f-42e6c38b2787", "type": "concept", "title": "Look development, palettes, contrast curves, highlight rolloff, color separation, and texture"}, {"id": "07fb5995-3ba1-4655-bdfe-3ff850a048c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Mood, continuity, memory, subjectivity, realism, stylization, and restraint"}, {"id": "621ace62-0543-4449-ae7e-5ddd7e4d4656", "type": "concept", "title": "Director/cinematographer collaboration and grading references"}], "description": "Students learn how color supports genre, emotion, period, point of view, and visual consistency."}, {"id": "eb02e5cc-dbfb-4070-85c9-983844658997", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Finishing pipeline", "children": [{"id": "c31a2f2c-dfee-4ac6-a262-43bad5825c44", "type": "concept", "title": "Conform from XML/AAF/EDL, relinking camera originals, handles, and timeline prep"}, {"id": "920cda81-7bf4-4df2-882a-a240c33caea0", "type": "concept", "title": "Titles, graphics, VFX shots, stabilization, reframing, and final picture polish"}, {"id": "07b4fb4b-5071-4ab2-ae59-6318e58e623f", "type": "concept", "title": "QC for flash frames, bad frames, dead pixels, illegal levels, and format errors"}], "description": "This section connects color to conform, online edit, final exports, and quality control."}]}, {"id": "ca5c4f17-73bf-407c-9080-cfefbcf61344", "type": "topic", "title": "Titles, Motion Graphics, VFX Handoffs, and Compositing", "description": "Students learn how graphics and effects support story, identity, information, accessibility, and professional finishing.", "children": [{"id": "83914dc7-9665-4729-8d81-f52aa112bb09", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Titles and information design", "children": [{"id": "768b40a5-854e-495a-8e80-aef122e33cae", "type": "concept", "title": "Main titles, lower thirds, end credits, intertitles, captions, cards, and subtitles"}, {"id": "8af6a4c4-feb2-401f-86ed-37f9f77aeb1c", "type": "concept", "title": "Typography, legibility, safe areas, motion, timing, hierarchy, and brand identity"}, {"id": "1ee74a50-7184-456d-8fc2-68e34fc2d089", "type": "concept", "title": "Credit order, legal names, music credits, and festival/online norms"}], "description": "This subtopic treats titles as part of storytelling, hierarchy, and viewer orientation."}, {"id": "f888f1db-03a3-4cac-ab9f-a456accf1145", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Motion graphics and basic compositing", "children": [{"id": "c3c35ee5-005a-472f-b4e7-6440e41a37e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Keyframes, masks, tracking, mattes, rotoscoping concepts, green screen, and cleanup"}, {"id": "72c67513-2485-40bc-b022-f16030b27466", "type": "concept", "title": "After Effects, Fusion, dynamic links, rendered graphics, and round-trip workflows"}, {"id": "89eee8a7-5593-464d-ad77-c95ce7966563", "type": "concept", "title": "When to solve in the NLE and when to hand off to motion/VFX"}], "description": "Students learn the practical bridge between editing and motion/VFX work."}, {"id": "b4dd05e8-5f6d-426f-a4a0-acd87997f415", "type": "subtopic", "title": "VFX turnover and review", "children": [{"id": "a897c9ed-dd57-4b7c-8448-a045d5498dec", "type": "concept", "title": "Temp comps, plates, handles, reference exports, shot IDs, frame ranges, and naming"}, {"id": "48297771-fc0e-4417-9985-3ae8709fa716", "type": "concept", "title": "VFX pulls, pull lists, annotations, review links, notes, and approvals"}, {"id": "6dc1cfc6-8f0f-4fbf-85f7-eb88374e49b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Versioning, shot status, final inserts, and conform checks"}], "description": "This section explains how editors communicate clearly with artists and producers during visual-effects work."}]}, {"id": "32188ca4-50fe-4088-9adc-973a1cfff4b9", "type": "topic", "title": "Collaboration, Review, Versioning, and Post Supervision", "description": "Students learn how professional post-production runs as a collaborative process involving editors, directors, producers, sound, color, VFX, and clients.", "children": [{"id": "f835b63d-b641-45de-9584-01d251acd7e2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Editorial collaboration", "children": [{"id": "606ad39b-fb28-4906-b450-7ffeab3c5c4e", "type": "concept", "title": "Director's cut, producer notes, client notes, peer critique, and test screening feedback"}, {"id": "d3f2cb5f-f1a3-47da-950a-bfa1467476b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Notes triage, creative diplomacy, problem diagnosis, and alternative versions"}, {"id": "25ce60c8-664d-4053-8c39-1bfbf771b950", "type": "concept", "title": "Communicating editorial rationale with clarity and humility"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches students to receive notes without losing the project's core intention."}, {"id": "f31899fe-1505-435d-a10d-effddd496cf5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Versioning and review systems", "children": [{"id": "6b6e6526-a69c-46d4-ac95-ccc17ebf52d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Version naming, date stamps, cut numbers, exports, review links, and change logs"}, {"id": "20a0651b-82a9-4ce1-896d-cd5fbf9274b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Frame.io-style review, timecoded comments, compare versions, and approvals"}, {"id": "4e9272bf-a07d-4851-ab48-63c50f81027f", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding overwritten timelines, lost media, and unclear handoffs"}], "description": "Students learn why disciplined versioning protects both creativity and deadlines."}, {"id": "cc1a51ac-c0c3-4d85-9536-ce5fc9134ce1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Post schedules and supervision", "children": [{"id": "cfcd90b4-edce-469e-9ffe-d998048839e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Assembly, rough cut, fine cut, lock, turnover, color, mix, VFX, QC, and delivery milestones"}, {"id": "b944423a-01b0-46f7-bf85-f937491d107a", "type": "concept", "title": "Roles: editor, assistant editor, post producer, colorist, sound editor, mixer, online editor, VFX supervisor"}, {"id": "ec80ee1c-283f-45d4-9224-86f96c6ec6fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Budget, scope, deadlines, revisions, festival needs, and client deliverables"}], "description": "This section builds professional awareness of the whole post calendar and its dependencies."}]}, {"id": "b21884a9-5de4-4464-acb8-59fa86504131", "type": "topic", "title": "Finishing, Delivery, Accessibility, Distribution, and Archiving", "description": "Students learn how to transform a creative cut into technically correct deliverables for screenings, web, festivals, clients, and archives.", "children": [{"id": "f7fb8d7a-9fa6-4721-aee7-f0f934a17556", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Export, codecs, and deliverables", "children": [{"id": "1af07b69-2791-4277-931b-78c132efff8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Containers, codecs, bitrates, frame rates, resolution, aspect ratio, color space, and audio specs"}, {"id": "75b22597-133b-4f57-a89f-35aa25b4b7e1", "type": "concept", "title": "H.264/H.265, ProRes, DNxHR/DNxHD, WAV, DCP basics, and social-platform exports"}, {"id": "bdd750b8-29f5-42cf-9405-9d7564bc5496", "type": "concept", "title": "Masters, screeners, review copies, textless versions, stems, and project archives"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces delivery as a professional craft with real consequences for playback, quality, and acceptance."}, {"id": "aea99de9-6491-4c17-bb1e-03c4940526dd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accessibility and localization", "children": [{"id": "251e2c0b-9eda-4ed8-bba4-647a43fadfbf", "type": "concept", "title": "Closed captions, open captions, subtitles, SDH, transcripts, and audio description"}, {"id": "dc01724f-8c4f-4d30-bf31-41f62bebe2d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Caption timing, reading speed, speaker IDs, sound cues, and quality checks"}, {"id": "e4eb4ef8-0e7e-48b1-be52-d6faf973d2f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Localization workflow, burned-in text, textless masters, and translation review"}], "description": "Students learn that professional media delivery includes viewers who need captions, subtitles, audio description, and language access."}, {"id": "1da43ac1-230b-4bcd-9913-8edb7aff4f5b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quality control and archiving", "children": [{"id": "5b61bc9d-e5a9-4367-8ac2-161d0b6550ed", "type": "concept", "title": "QC watchdown, flash frames, sync, audio peaks, clipping, title errors, and missing shots"}, {"id": "6ece7db7-eb89-43a6-a4d8-3b14927d1ebd", "type": "concept", "title": "Metadata, release forms, cue sheets, rights documents, project files, and media maps"}, {"id": "ed4e7893-0229-4053-9b97-311c9846d289", "type": "concept", "title": "Long-term storage, drive labels, cloud backups, migration, and portfolio exports"}], "description": "This section teaches students to check and preserve their work like professionals."}]}, {"id": "1171f7ea-aa03-4fa6-9b5c-f1d90dcff97c", "type": "topic", "title": "Complete Project Capstone: Rough Cut to Locked Picture", "description": "Students synthesize story, workflow, sound, color, graphics, collaboration, and delivery into a polished short project.", "children": [{"id": "da7c7dc5-8c23-4f85-b57e-3c5e21f45be1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Assembly, rough cut, and fine cut", "children": [{"id": "d206a56e-9044-492b-8acf-fd9166e97b27", "type": "concept", "title": "Assembly cut, rough cut, fine cut, picture lock, and final polish"}, {"id": "49227012-ab3f-4956-9cc9-2fcc5b0fe845", "type": "concept", "title": "Cut goals, edit decision list, revision priorities, and faculty/peer notes"}, {"id": "67583f97-5065-433a-b14c-c63fa04c61e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintaining continuity between creative intent and technical workflow"}], "description": "The capstone follows a real post sequence so students experience editing as iterative problem solving."}, {"id": "0dcad079-316e-42b8-a27b-2b0a402c261b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integrated post package", "children": [{"id": "31dd5ba8-7dfc-4a28-8642-bc18e66b1ac2", "type": "concept", "title": "Sound edit, temp mix or final mix, color correction, grade, titles, credits, and graphics"}, {"id": "0afe65c8-8b69-4f27-ac92-58e1b28a78e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Final exports, captions or subtitles, QC checklist, poster frame, and thumbnail"}, {"id": "015671ee-a568-4c78-8b10-a468fdbc6d8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Archive folder, media map, project file, release/rights notes, and deliverables log"}], "description": "Students combine the specialized skills of the course into one coherent professional package."}, {"id": "5de3272d-4d4e-4a3b-bb38-c3e4902048aa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critique, reflection, and portfolio presentation", "children": [{"id": "e02de3ae-dc0a-41a8-9dcd-4fa1cf521b3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Screening critique, audience response, director/editor statement, and revision reflection"}, {"id": "f25f0bc6-b6f4-401e-afdf-db3938f9381e", "type": "concept", "title": "Before/after examples, scene breakdowns, workflow screenshots, and portfolio excerpts"}, {"id": "8cc0e706-4c81-460d-ba3c-c6cee408959a", "type": "concept", "title": "Lessons learned, collaboration notes, and next-step goals"}], "description": "This subtopic turns the final project into evidence of craft growth and professional readiness."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$edpojson$::jsonb,
